UPDATE public.designers SET biography = $bio$Alex Proba is a German-born, New York-based multidisciplinary artist and designer whose exuberant patterns and swirling organic forms have made her one of the most sought-after creative voices in contemporary design. Founded in 2013 while she was still working as an art director for Nike, Studio Proba has since expanded across product, graphic, environmental and furniture design — transforming every possible surface into a canvas for joy.

Proba studied spatial and graphic design at the Akademie Mode und Design in Berlin and the Gerrit Rietveld Academie in Amsterdam before moving to New York, where she worked in branding and art direction for Kickstarter and Nike. In 2018 she committed full-time to her studio after a personal project — 'A Poster a Day', in which she designed one poster every day for a year — went viral and attracted international attention. A second long-form series, 'A Pool a Day', re-imagined the swimming pool as a graphic canvas and became the foundation for her later architectural commissions.

<strong>'I never sketch. I go straight to the computer and just start. The shapes come from an emotional place — I design how I feel.'</strong> — Alex Proba, Galerie Magazine interview


https://youtu.be/6o-b80DxkzE | Alex Proba, Multi-Disciplinary Designer and Creative Director - The Second Studio podcast 2021

Her collaboration with <a href="/designers/cc-tapis">CC-Tapis</a>, the Milan-based maker of hand-knotted contemporary rugs, produced 'The One or The Other' collection — a series of rugs that translate Proba's signature abstract landscapes into Himalayan wool and silk. Unveiled during Milan Design Week, each design pulses with her distinctive palette of warm terracottas, deep blues and painterly gradients, hand-knotted in Nepal by master artisans. The CC-Tapis partnership built on earlier textile work for Maharam Digital Projects, whose archive places her among contemporaries such as Hella Jongerius, Paul Smith and Sarah Morris.

Beyond textiles, Proba's practice spans murals, ceramics, furniture and large-scale environmental installations. Her commercial collaborators include Nike, Adidas, Samsung, IKEA Art Event, Areaware, Bolia, Poketo, Urban Outfitters, West Elm, Calico Wallpaper and Slowdown Studio, for whom she has produced throws, wallpapers, homeware and limited-edition objects. Architectural commissions include the Fernandez Residence pool in Miami, a tiled mural for an Adidas flagship store, and façade and interior works for hospitality clients across the United States and Europe. Her studio has also been commissioned by Sundance, MoMA Design Store and Kickstarter.

Proba's work has been exhibited at Sight Unseen Offsite in New York, The Future Perfect, Colony, NYCxDesign and at fairs and galleries in Milan, Los Angeles and Dubai. Editorial coverage spans Architectural Digest, Wallpaper*, The New York Times, Dezeen, Galerie Magazine, Sight Unseen and Frame, and her studio has been profiled as one of the defining post-digital design practices of the 2010s and 2020s.


https://res.cloudinary.com/dif1oamtj/image/upload/v1780132503/Screenshot_2026-05-30_at_5.13.19_PM_rra6z4.png | Tile Mural Design - The Fernandez Residence Pool

<strong>With a practice that defies categorisation, Alex Proba has redefined the relationship between fine art and functional design — proving that colour, pattern and instinct can transform the most utilitarian surfaces into sources of daily wonder.</strong>$bio$
